<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Senegal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Senegal is a region of westernmost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, named after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal-river">Senegal River</a> and now an independent country. It was home to states such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jolof-empire">Jolof Empire</a> and was a frontier of the Almoravid movement and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a>. It later became the core of French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaabu-empire">Kaabu Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a> profiles refer to developments in the region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/senegal.jpg" alt="Senegal" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original upload by Nightstallion · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Senegal.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
